{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"printf '%s\\\\n' '--- fuzz-eval.C ---'; sed -n '1,240p' fuzz/fuzz-eval.C; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- nearby project metadata ---'; ls -la; find . -name AGENTS.md -print; printf '%s\\\\n' '--- eval references ---'; rg -n --hidden --glob '\"'!build/**'\"' --glob '\"'!out/**'\"' 'fuzz-eval|Eval|eval|evaluate|parse' fuzz src include lib 2>/dev/null | head -240\"","aggregated_output":"--- fuzz-eval.C ---\n/*\n * Copyright (C) 2023 Emweb bv, Herent, Belgium.\n *\n * See the LICENSE file for terms of use.\n */\n\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <stddef.h>\n#include <string>\n\n#include \"Wt/Exception/WInvalidFormatException.h\"\n#include \"Wt/Exception/WInvalidOperationException.h\"\n\n#include <Wt/WMessageResources.h>\n\n#define kMinInputLength 10\n#define kMaxInputLength 5120\n\nnamespace {\n  int eval(std::string expression, ::uint64_t n)\n  {\n    try {\n      return Wt::WMessageResources::evalPluralCase(expression, n);\n    } catch (Wt::WInvalidFormatException& ife) {\n    } catch (Wt::WInvalidOperationException& ioe) {\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nextern \"C\" int LLVMFuzzerTestOneInput(const uint8_t *Data, size_t Size) {\n\n    if (Size < kMinInputLength || Size > kMaxInputLength) {\n        return 1;\n    }\n\n    std::string input(Data, Data + Size);\n    eval(input, 0);\n\n    return 0;\n}\n--- nearby project metadata ---\ntotal 824\ndrwxr-xr-x 15 root root   4096 Oct 18 07:15 .\ndrwxrwxrwx  1 root root   4096 Oct 18 07:15 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003    797 Apr 30  2025 .dprint.json\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003    129 Apr 30  2025 .editorconfig\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003     19 Apr 30  2025 .eslintignore\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003    950 Apr 30  2025 .eslintrc.yml\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003    361 Apr 30  2025 .gitignore\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 root root   4096 Oct 18 07:15 .vscode\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003    858 Apr 30  2025 BUILD.md\n-rw-r--r--  1 1002 1003  21838 Apr 30  2025 CMakeLists.txt\n-rw-r