{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"reasoning","text":"**Exploring vulnerability issues**\n\nI’m looking into a potential vulnerability involving WException construction and catch behavior. It seems like passing by value might lead to double freeing issues. Existing checks throw and catch exceptions, but I wonder why the original fuzzer might have a known bug related to it. The parameter type being a reference could be a culprit for copied exceptions. A patch might be necessary to prevent throwing WInvalidFormatException. I’ll take time to inspect the WException definitions further to find the root cause."}}
