{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_55","type":"reasoning","text":"**Considering parser issues**\n\nI'm thinking about the parser and how it might hang due to zero division or issues with grammar exception handling. I want to be cautious about using a malformed parser. If the patch doesn't handle the exception correctly, it may lead to unexpected behavior. I should stick with the more reliable existing parser for now. However, if I implement stage 2, I hope it can pass without causing any problems. Restoring it should be the priority."}}
